IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc18-forfeiture`

-- ccc18-tests-forfeiture.l4 -- tests for ccc18-forfeiture.l4. Expected values are written from the text of the Criminal Code
-- (R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, lines 10275-10956 of the plain-text rendering), beside each assertion, and not copied from the module's own output.

-- 490.1(1): conviction (or a section 730 discharge) of an indictable offence under the Code or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the Attorney General's application, and the court's satisfaction on a balance of probabilities.
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not convicted
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not offence-related property
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the keel's answer is not covered
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited` FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the first limb fails whatever the keel says
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the Crown in whose right the property is forfeited` TRUE EQUALS `s 490.1(1)(a) Her Majesty in right of the province, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the Attorney General or Solicitor General of that province`
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the Crown in whose right the property is forfeited` FALSE EQUALS `s 490.1(1)(b) Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the member of the Privy Council for Canada designated by the Governor in Council`
-- subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the property is returned under 490.4(3)
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court decides under 490.41(3) not to forfeit
#ASSERT `s 490.1(1) the court shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no time is stated; the court orders the forfeiture: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.1(1) the duty of the court to order the forfeiture` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.1(1) order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.1(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) of property not shown to be related to the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.1(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) of property not shown to be related to the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: the evidence does not establish to the satisfaction of the court that the property is rela
#ASSERT `s 490.1(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) of property not shown to be related to the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: the court is satisfied, beyond a reasonable doubt, that the property is offence-related pr

#ASSERT `s 490.1(2.1) an order may be issued in respect of property situated outside Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.1(2.1) an order may be issued in respect of property situated outside Canada` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: the property is situated outside Canada

#ASSERT `s 490.1(3) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.1(3) a person convicted of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.1(3) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.1(3) the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.1(3) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.1(3) another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another person
#ASSERT `s 490.1(3) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.1(3) a person convicted of an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different decision
#ASSERT `s 490.1(3) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.1(3) the Attorney General` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a ground raising no question of law or mixed law and fact

#ASSERT `s 490.2(1) the Attorney General may make an application to a judge for an order of forfeiture` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.2(1) the Attorney General may make an application to a judge for an order of forfeiture` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: an information has been laid in respect of an indictable offence under this Act or the Cor
#ASSERT `s 490.2(1) the Attorney General may make an application to a judge for an order of forfeiture` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: the applicant is the Attorney General

#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) missing
#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) missing
#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c) missing: the accused has neither died nor absconded
#TRACE `s 490.2(2) the duty of the judge to order the forfeiture` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 490.2(2) order that the property be forfeited and disposed of in accordance with subsection (4)` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- returned under 490.4(3)
#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not forfeited under 490.41(3)
#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490.2(2) the judge shall order the property forfeited, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 490.2(3): a warrant issued on 1 January 2020: the six month period begins on that day and ends on 30 June 2020, the day of deemed absconding.
#ASSERT `s 490.2(3) the day on which the accused is deemed to have absconded` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 2020)
#ASSERT `s 490.2(3) the day on which the accused is deemed to have absconded` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 8 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 2 2021)   -- across a year end
#ASSERT `s 490.2(3) the day on which the accused is deemed to have absconded` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no information
#ASSERT `s 490.2(3) the day on which the accused is deemed to have absconded` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no warrant
#ASSERT `s 490.2(3) the day on which the accused is deemed to have absconded` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- attempts to arrest not unsuccessful throughout

#ASSERT `s 490.2(4) the Crown in whose right the judge shall order the property forfeited` TRUE EQUALS `s 490.1(1)(a) Her Majesty in right of the province, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the Attorney General or Solicitor General of that province`
#ASSERT `s 490.2(4) the Crown in whose right the judge shall order the property forfeited` FALSE EQUALS `s 490.1(1)(b) Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with by the member of the Privy Council for Canada designated by the Governor in Council`

#ASSERT `s 490.2(4.1) an order may be issued in respect of property situated outside Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.2(4.1) an order may be issued in respect of property situated outside Canada` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: the property is situated outside Canada

#ASSERT `s 490.2(5) judge` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.2(5) judge` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.2(5) judge` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490.2(5) judge` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.2(5) judge` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.3 the court may set aside the conveyance or transfer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.3 the court may set aside the conveyance or transfer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless": valuable consideration, good faith
#ASSERT `s 490.3 the court may set aside the conveyance or transfer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- before the seizure or restraint order
#ASSERT `s 490.3 the court may set aside the conveyance or transfer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 490.4(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.4(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.4(1) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.4(1) require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to the person` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.4(1) (hearing) the court may hear the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.4(1) (hearing) the court may hear the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: before making an order under subsection 490.1(1) or 490.2(2) in relation to the property, 

#ASSERT `s 490.4(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.4(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- without: (a) the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in t
#ASSERT `s 490.4(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- without: (b) the notice specifies the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set
#ASSERT `s 490.4(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- without: (c) the notice sets out the offence charged and a description of the property

#ASSERT `s 490.4(3) the court may order that the property be returned to the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.4(3) the court may order that the property be returned to the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person was charged
#ASSERT `s 490.4(3) the court may order that the property be returned to the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- took title from such a person to avoid forfeiture
#ASSERT `s 490.4(3) the court may order that the property be returned to the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not shown to be the lawful owner or entitled to possession
#ASSERT `s 490.4(3) the court may order that the property be returned to the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- does not appear innocent

#ASSERT `s 490.41(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person, and may hear them` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.41(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person, and may hear them` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a dwelling-house
#ASSERT `s 490.41(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person, and may hear them` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.41(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person, and may hear them` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- does not reside there
#ASSERT `s 490.41(1) the court shall require notice to be given to the person, and may hear them` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not of the immediate family
#TRACE `s 490.41(1) the duty of the court to require notice to the member of the immediate family` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.41(1) require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to the member of the immediate family who resides in the dwelling-house` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.41(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.41(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- without: (a) the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in t
#ASSERT `s 490.41(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- without: (b) the notice specifies the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set
#ASSERT `s 490.41(2) the notice is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- without: (c) the notice sets out the offence charged and a description of the property

#ASSERT `s 490.41(3) (decision) the court may decide not to order the forfeiture of the property or part of the property` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.41(3) (decision) the court may decide not to order the forfeiture of the property or part of the property` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: the court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490

#ASSERT `s 490.41(3) (restraint order) the court may revoke a restraint order made in respect of the property or part of it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.41(3) (restraint order) the court may revoke a restraint order made in respect of the property or part of it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- without: the court is satisfied that the impact of an order of forfeiture made under subsection 490

#ASSERT `s 490.41(4) the court shall also consider the matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 490.41(4)(a) the impact of an order of forfeiture on any member of the immediate family of the person charged with or convicted of the offence, if the dwelling-house was the member’s principal residence at the time the charge was laid and continues to be the member’s principal residence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.41(4) the court shall also consider the matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 490.41(4)(b) whether the member referred to in paragraph (a) appears innocent of any complicity in the offence or of any collusion in relation to the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.41(4) the court shall also consider the matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 490.41(4) a matter outside paragraphs (a) and (b)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.41(4) the court shall also consider the matter` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `s 490.41(4)(b) whether the member referred to in paragraph (a) appears innocent of any complicity in the offence or of any collusion in relation to the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not making a decision under (3)
#ASSERT `s 490.41(4) the court shall also consider the matter` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `s 490.41(4)(b) whether the member referred to in paragraph (a) appears innocent of any complicity in the offence or of any collusion in relation to the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a dwelling-house
#ASSERT `s 490.41(4) the court shall also consider the matter` NOTHING TRUE `s 490.41(4)(b) whether the member referred to in paragraph (a) appears innocent of any complicity in the offence or of any collusion in relation to the offence` EQUALS NOTHING

-- 490.5(1): forfeited on 1 March 2020; thirty days after is 31 March 2020 (the day of the forfeiture is in time: fork F3).
#ASSERT `s 490.5(1) the person may apply for an order under subsection (4)` `s 490.5(1) an order under subsection 490.1(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 31 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thirtieth day
